      "title": "Two ways to alarm on the same data",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Left:** the alarms Node-RED records in the `alarm` table — one per rule breach, at most one a minute per code (deduplication).\n\n**Right:** the Grafana alert rules — evaluated on a clock, with a pending period and a decision about what to do when no data arrives."
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Node-RED alarms (newest first)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
        "uid": "seda_lab_postgresql"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
            "uid": "seda_lab_postgresql"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "editorMode": "code",
          "format": "table",
          "rawSql": "SELECT a.ts AS \"time (UTC)\", c.code AS component, a.code AS alarm, a.severity, a.message FROM alarm a JOIN component c ON c.id = a.component_id ORDER BY a.ts DESC LIMIT 20"
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 12,
        "w": 14,
